I go to a large vegetable stall.
There is a big crowd here.
Fresh red tomatoes are kept there.
I point towards the tomatoes.
I ask, "Bhaiya, how much is a kilo of tomatoes?"
The vegetable vendor says, "Madam, forty rupees a kilo."
I do not need many tomatoes.
I say, "Please give me half a kilo of tomatoes."
The vendor sorts out some good tomatoes.
He puts them on the weighing scale.
He weighs the tomatoes.
Then he puts the tomatoes in my bag.
I ask, "Bhaiya, how much is it in total?"
He says, "Twenty rupees, Madam."
I take out twenty rupees from my purse.
I give the money to the vendor.
He smiles and says thank you to me.
